{"step_index":948,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T11:27:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T11:27:47Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T11:27:47Z\nShowing lines 40-89 of 89\n40: - Post-change evidence: exported private key derives the live router public key `4V4Wob4v8YxCcQ4nz95Jt3b/aQcAInLq+ABIvvS7/Qg=`; `uci export network` is byte-identical to the backup; `wg show` reports a handshake 74 seconds earlier; `ip route get 10.0.0.2` selects `wgdecoy`, source `10.0.0.9`; ping receives 3/3 replies; native wget of `http://10.0.0.2:8080/` exits 0. Authenticated application flow and router reboot were not exercised. No `oi` command exists on this router; native `ip` commands were used. `stat` is also absent, so permissions were verified using `ls -ld`.\n41: \n42: ## Panel-assisted auth diagnosis (2026-10-21, `panel-auth-20261021`)\n43: \n44: - **Confirmed failure boundary:** a fresh OIA1 obtained through the actual router `10.0.0.9` WireGuard path, forwarded unchanged by the existing UI `DoorClient`, reached the same-origin connector at `http://10.0.0.2:8080`. The first normal bootstrap read, `project.get_context` / `chat.context`, returned `UNAUTHENTICATED` with raw detail `Assigned%20browser%20identity%20unavailable`. The UI client's automatic `register_key` fallback was deliberately not invoked. This was the real UI transport executed on the main host, not a capture of the user's browser.\n45: - **Issuer works for that path:** router route selects `wgdecoy`, source `10.0.0.9`; issuer returns HTTP200, `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://10.0.0.2:8080`, and an OIA1 document with a credential present and advertised door `https://10.0.0.2:8090`. No assertion/SID1/private key was logged or persisted.\n46: - **Source explanation, not an inner-error receipt:** `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/interceptor.rs:529-536` maps every `validate_bound_oracle` failure to this exact public error. Lines50-108 check the assigned stored session, authored SID1